pylsl (1.18.2-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Initial Debian/NeuroDebian packaging.
    Not in Debian, Ubuntu or NeuroDebian; upstream ships only PyPI wheels that
    bundle a private copy of liblsl.
  * Pure-Python ctypes binding; depends on the packaged system liblsl
    (liblsl2) found at runtime via ctypes.util.find_library, instead of the
    bundled library shipped in upstream wheels.
  * Build with pybuild; version supplied via SETUPTOOLS_SCM_PRETEND_VERSION.

 -- Morgan Hough <morgan.hough@gmail.com>  Sun, 21 Jun 2026 16:10:00 -0700
